    "title": "Pope Leo XIV Has Hilarious Comeback to Trolling Cubs Fan at the Vatican - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kayla Aldecoa ,\n1 hours ago\nPope Leo XIV proved his loyalty to the Chicago White Sox after being trolled by a Cubs fan at the Vatican.\n\"Go Cubs!\" one man shouted to the passing Pope Mobile on Wednesday, October 15.\nPope Leo -- a native of the Windy City -- paused his papal wave to shout back, \"Han perdido!\"\n\"They lost!\" the religious leader translated.\nThe Chicago Cubs lost to the Milwaukee Brewers in Game 5 of the NLDS last week, a heartbreaking end to their successful season.\nThe video quickly went viral as fans couldn't believe the leader of the Catholic church was so in the know on current sporting events.\n\"As a Cubs fan I don’t like this. As a fan of people being genuine and true and loyal, I love it,\" one social media user tweeted in response to the White Sox sharing the clip.\n\"Cubs fans about to boycott church now lol,\" another joked. \"At least the Cubs were in the playoffs,\" yet another wrote, alluding to the White Sox having missed the playoffs for the fourth year in a row.\nAfter Pope Leo was selected as the first American leader of the Catholic church earlier this year, the Chicago Cubs quickly claimed him as their own. However, his brother, John Prevost, clarified, \"He was never, ever a Cubs fan .\"\n“Whoever said Cubs on the radio got it wrong,\" John Prevost said. \"It’s Sox.\"",
